  "evaluation": "All three correctly classify the disagreement as genuine and identify population as the strongest explanation: older CKD patients versus younger adults treated for depression and healthy controls. Neither study provides an explicit basis for calling the null underpowered or the outcomes fundamentally different. C gives the clearest account of both observational findings and their population contrast. A is similarly accurate but less explicit about the findings. B is close, though “general psychiatric patients” is less precise than patients treated for depression, and its detail loosely attributes the patient group's mean age to the controls as well.",
  "ranking": ["C", "A", "B"]
}
